+# Incident brief: August and September 2026
+
+Follow-up status as of the 30 September meeting.
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall, full database disk
+
+**Impact:** incoming data stopped for about 2.5 hours overnight; customers saw stale dashboards. No data was lost.
+
+**Cause:** one malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs filled the database disk, blocking writes.
+
+**Fix:** restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then freed disk space.
+
+Follow-ups:
+- Disk alert at 80% (Sunil): done.
+- Stop bad batches jamming ingest (Jonas): open, in review.
+- Paging escalation (no named owner): done; unanswered pages pass to secondary, then manager, after 15 minutes.
+
+## 21 September: expired API certificate
+
+**Impact:** public API down 47 minutes on a Monday morning; nearly all customers and browsers could not connect.
+
+**Cause:** the security certificate expired; its automatic renewal had failed silently all month on an outdated access token.
+
+**Fix:** renewed the certificate and restarted the API; renewal failures now raise an alert.
+
+Follow-ups:
+- Reminder 14 days before each expiry (Priya): done.
+- Alert on days until expiry (Priya): open.
+- Expiry check in weekly checklist (Tomasz): open.
+- Incident handlers record their steps while working (Mara): done.
